82,0,RTEX node addressing error,"On power up of the control power, node address setting rotary switch on the servo drive has been set to a value outside the valid value.",Check the setting of the node address setting switch.
,,,,Set node address setting switch to a value within the range of 0 and 31 and then turn on control power to the servo driver.
83,0,RTEX continues communication error 1,An error (CRC error) with reading data received by a local node continued for a specified period.,Check the communication cable for excessive noise.
,,,,"Check the communication cable for length, layout arrangement and connections."
,,,,Communication cable must be category 5-e or higher (6 or higher grade is recommended) shielded twisted pair cable (STPC) specified by TIA/EIA-568.
,,,,"Replace the cable with the one recommended as above, if not a recommended one."
,,,,Attach the ferrite core to the cable if effective.
83,1,RTEX continues communication error 2,An error with the reading data received by a local node continued for a specified period.,Check the communication cable for excessive noise.
,,,"Note) This alarm assumes an error if CRC error, receiving failure, or cyclic data error occurs.","Check the communication cable for length, layout arrangement and connections."
,,,,Communication cable must be category 5-e or higher (6 or higher grade is recommended) shielded twisted pair cable (STPC) specified by TIA/EIA-568.
,,,,"Replace the cable with the one recommended as above, if not a recommended one."
,,,,Attach the ferrite core to the cable if effective.
84,0,RTEX communication timeout error,No communication data was received and no signal to start receive interrupt handling was received from MNM1221 (RTEX communication control ASIC) for a specified period.,Check to see that the cable is disconnected or broken.
,,,,"Check that the upstream node is ready for transmission (power is ON, not reset)."
,,,,Make sure that the host device can transmit the signal at the correct timing and speed.
,,,,The communication cycle set by Pr7.20 (RTEX communication period) must match the transmission cycle of the host device.
,,,,Check the communication cable for excessive noise.
,,,,"Check the communication cable for length, layout arrangement and connections."
,,,,Communication cable must be category 5-e or higher (6 or higher grade is recommended) shielded twisted pair cable (STPC) specified by TIA/EIA-568.
,,,,"Replace the cable with the one recommended as above, if not a recommended one."
,,,,Attach the ferrite core to the cable if effective.
84,3,REX sync & initialization error,Error occurred during communication and servo sync and initialization process.,"Turn off the power once, then re-enter. If error repeats, this might be a failure."
,,,,"Stop using the products, and replace the motor and the driver. Return the products to the dealer or manufacturer."
84,5,RTEX communication cycle error,"Although the NMNI221 (RTEX communication control ASIC) output a receive interrupt handling start signal, communication and servo went out of synchronizationdue to an output frequency problem with the signal.",Make sure that the host device can transmit the signal at the correct timing and speed.
,,,,The communication cycle set by Pr7.20 (RTEX communication period) must match the transmission cycle of the host device.
,,,,Check the communication cable for excessive noise.
,,,,"Check the communication cable for length, layout arrangement and connections."
,,,,Communication cable must be category 5-e or higher (6 or higher grade is recommended) shielded twisted pair cable (STPC) specified by TIA/EIA-568.
,,,,"Replace the cable with the one recommended as above, if not a recommended one."
,,,,Attach the ferrite core to the cable if effective.
86,0,RTEX cyclic-data not receivable 1,"A problem with the data (C/R and MAC-ID) in the cyclic command area, or a problem with the Sub_Chk in 32-byte 86 mode continued for a specified period.",Check the data in the cyclic command field (MAC-ID or C/R).
,,,,Check process performed on the host device.
86,1,RTEX cyclic-data not receivable 2,A problem with cyclic command code continued for a specified period.,Check the data in the cyclic command field (cyclic command).
,,,,Check process performed on the host device.
86,2,RTEX_Update_Counter error,The setup value for Pr7.38 (RTEX_Update_Counter error protection setup) has been exceeded and the Update_Counter has not been updated correctly.,Check for any trouble in the process performed on the host device.
,,,,Check if there is any problem in frequency setting in upper devise side and in amplifier side.
,,,,Increase the setup value for Pr7.38.
,,,,"When Update_Counter is not used with ratio of communication frequency and command renewal frequency being 1:1, this alarm is made invalid."
87,0,강제 알람 입력 보호,강제 알람 입력(E-STOP)이 입력됨.,강제 알람 입력(E-STOP) 배선을 확인한다.
90,2,RTEX multi-axis synchronization establishment error,Communication error occurred or communication was lost during transition to synchronization establishment in full synchronization mode.,Check the communication cable for excessive noise.
,,,,"Check the communication cable for length, layout arrangement and connections."
,,,,Communication cable must be category 5-e or higher (6 or higher grade is recommended) shielded twisted pair cable (STPC) specified by TIA/EIA-568.
,,,,"Replace the cable with the one recommended as above, if not a recommended one."
,,,,Attach the ferrite core to the cable if effective.
91,1,RTEX command error,"Inconsistency in communication frequency, semi-close/full-close, and combination of 16/32 byte mode and control mode.",Check the process of upper device for any problem.
,,,Control mode was switched at intervals shorter than 2 ms.,
,,,"Control mode was changed during profile position latch positioning/profile home position return (Type_Code = 12h, 13h, 31h, 32h, 33h).",
,,,Control mode was changed while non-cyclic command (Busy = 1) was processed.,
,,,"Home position return command (4h) was executed during profile position latch positioning/profile home position return (Type_Code = 12h, 13h, 31h, 32h, 33h).",
,,,"Initialization mode (Type_Code = 1??h, 31h) for home position return command (4h) was performed during profile positioning/profile continuous rotation (Type_Code = 10h, 11h, 20h).",
,,,Type_Code was changed during profile position control (pp).,
,,,Type_Code = 1*h/2*h for home position return command (4th) was performed at the time of speed control (CV)/torque control (CT).,
92,1,Feedback scale data recovery error,"When in the absolute mode (absolute scale), internal position data has not been correctly initialized.",Regulate the power source of the feedback scale to 5VDC ±5% (4.75?5.25V).…Measure the voltage at the feedback scale connection cable end if it is long.
,,,,"If the motor cable and feedback scale connection cable are bundled together, separated them."
,,,,Connect the shield to FG.…See the feedback scale connection diagramin.
93,0,Parameter setup error 1,Electronic gear ratio exceeds the allowable range.,Check the setting value of the parameter.
,,,,Electronic gear ratio must be in the range 1/1000 to 1000.
93,2,Parameter setup error 2,Feedback scale ratio exceeds acceptable range.,Check the setting value of the parameter.
,,,,Feedback scale ratio must be in the range 1/40 to 160.
93,3,Feedback scale connection error,The communication type of the connected external scale (serial communication model) does not match the type selected through Pr3.23 (Feedback scale selection).,Set Pr3.23 (Feedback scale selection) to the type of feedback scale connected.
93,5,Parameter setup error 4,The combination conditions of Pr7.20 (RTEX communication period) and Pr7.21 (RTEX command update period) are not met.,Check settings of the parameters.
,,,Feed forward settings of Pr7.35?Pr7.37 are duplicated.,"For correct setting conditions, refer to the technical document, Specification of RTEX communication."
94,2,Home position return error,An error with profile home position return occurred.,Check sensor installation status etc. for any problem.
95,0,모터 자동 인식 이상 보호,모터와 서보 앰프가 매치되지 않음.,취급 설명서에 기재된 서보 앰프와 모터를 올바르게 조합하여 사용한다.
95,1,모터 자동 인식 이상 보호,모터와 서보 앰프가 매치되지 않음.,취급 설명서에 기재된 서보 앰프와 모터를 올바르게 조합하여 사용한다.
95,2,모터 자동 인식 이상 보호,모터와 서보 앰프가 매치되지 않음.,취급 설명서에 기재된 서보 앰프와 모터를 올바르게 조합하여 사용한다.
95,3,모터 자동 인식 이상 보호,모터와 서보 앰프가 매치되지 않음.,취급 설명서에 기재된 서보 앰프와 모터를 올바르게 조합하여 사용한다.
95,4,모터 자동 인식 이상 보호,모터와 서보 앰프가 매치되지 않음.,취급 설명서에 기재된 서보 앰프와 모터를 올바르게 조합하여 사용한다.
96,0,(MNM1223 이상),제어 회로가 과대한 노이즈 등으로 오작동함. 서보 앰프의 자기 진단 기능이 작동하고 서보 앰프 내부에 어떤 이상이 발생.,"전원을 끄고 다시 켠다. 그래도 표시가 나타나고 에러가 발생하는 경우에는 고장일 가능성이 있습니다. 사용을 중지하고 모터, 서보 앰프를 교환하십시오."
97,0,(제어 모드 설정 이상),제어 회로가 과대한 노이즈 등으로 오작동함. 서보 앰프의 자기 진단 기능이 작동하고 서보 앰프 내부에 어떤 이상이 발생.,"전원을 끄고 다시 켠다. 그래도 표시가 나타나고 에러가 발생하는 경우에는 고장일 가능성이 있습니다. 사용을 중지하고 모터, 서보 앰프를 교환하십시오."
